ces tool doesn\'t require any arguments, as per the description. So the tool call should just be the name of the tool with empty arguments. Let me make sure I\'m not missing anything. The function\'s parameters are an empty object, so the arguments JSON should be {}.\n\nWait, the user\'s instructions say that for each function call, I need to return a JSON object with the function name and arguments within the tool_call tags. Since get_services has no parameters, the arguments are an empty object. So the correct tool call is {"name": "get_services", "arguments": {}}. That should retrieve the list of service names from Grafana. I think that\'s all. No other parameters needed here. Let me double-check the tool\'s description. Yes, the Args section is empty, so no arguments are required. Alright, that\'s the correct call.\n</think>\n\n', additional_kwargs={'tool_calls': [{'function': {'arguments': '{}', 'name': 'get_services'}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-abe1324b780dbb86', 'type': 'function'}], 'provider_specific_fields': {'reasoning': None, 'refusal': None}}, response_metadata={'token_usage': {'completion_tokens': 237, 'prompt_tokens': 2481, 'total_tokens': 2718, 'completion_tokens_details': None, 'prompt_tokens_details': None}, 'model': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B', 'finish_reason': 'tool_calls', 'logprobs': None, 'model_name': 'openai/Qwen/Qwen3-8B'}, id='lc_run--019cfb93-97a2-70e1-8002-39355ce53429-0', tool_calls=[{'name': 'get_services', 'args': {}, 'id': 'chatcmpl-tool-abe1324b780dbb86', 'type': 'tool_call'}], invalid_tool_calls=[], usage_metadata={'input_tokens': 2481, 'output_tokens': 237, 'total_tokens': 2718}), ToolMessage(content='meta=None content=[TextContent(type=\'text\', text="[\'frontend\', \'product-catalog\', \'product-reviews\', \'checkout\', \'recommendation\', \'quote\', \'ad\', \'load-generator\', \'email\', \'fraud-detection\', \'payment\', \'shipping\', \'image-provider\', \'frontend-proxy\', \'currency\', \'accounting\', \'jaeger-all-in-one\', \'cart\', \